bed nvim behaviour; the editor surfaces abort by name at the read; a shape is an optimization — a key the shape cannot hold goes to a hidden SIDE Map, never an abort; pcall never swallows a LuaBreak). The rest, every one a named break: loadstring 7 (Lua source built at run time), the editor 4, a script without its job file 1. The SEMANTICS oracle is `tests/luajs_spec.lua` (differential: Lua with the standard print vs the emitted JS under node, byte-identical). CART-1197 |\n| Declare HOW a Lua construct becomes JS as a PAIR OF EXAMPLES (not code) — the local half of the transliterator | `lua/cartograph/luajs/rules.lua` `M.RULES`: `{ lua = 'a + b', js = '$add(a, b)' }` — both sides READ by the lossless reader (`cartograph.algebraread`, the JS side as javascript), every Lua identifier a hole, the left MATCHED on a node's term modulo layout (gaps and comments dropped), the right INSTANTIATED and printed (algebra match / instantiate / cst_print); hole modes `as = { f = 'name' \\| 'raw' \\| 'block' }`; compile refuses a rule that drops a hole. 31 rules (literals, grouping, indexing, the operators, do, return 0/1); the CONTEXT cases (scope, calls, tables, loops, if, goto, number/string values) stay in `cartograph.luajs`. `algebraread.read_tree(src, lang, tree, visit)` gives each node of a caller's tree its term. `tools/luajs.lua` reports `RULES: n declared, m match(es); k never fired` (a rule no source reaches has no witness). Acceptance of the move: all 357 emitted files BYTE-IDENTICAL to the hand emitter; luajs_spec pins every rule firing — which then surfaced CART-1200 (no values returned ONE nil), fixed as a deliberate output change (`return $mv();`, normalized diff otherwise empty). CART-1199 |\n| Check the Lua→JS transliteration on EVERY program up to a size (not a sample) — control flow, value counts, coercions | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/luajsgen.lua <control\\|values\\|coercion> <max size> [corpus dir] [out dir] [min=<n>]` — `cartograph.luajs.gencheck`: ev