ready named `to`) is a `name-occupied` DECISION; accepted, the occupant moves to the placeholder `<to>__1` in the same plan and a `placeholder` residue says to choose its real name (CART-1009). Comment/string mentions: a counted `text-mentions` frontier, never rewritten. Replayed on CART-1160 step 7 (2203d17^): the same 3 reads + 3 keys, `binders` stopped as occupied. CART-1175 |\n| Deploy through a PLAN with review gates and a real undo (release, switch, health check; roll back on failure) | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/toolbelt.lua run deploy <root> from=<src dir> target=<deploy dir> [approve=yes] [rollback=1] [apply=1]` — the local deployment world (cartograph.deploy): `release` writes releases/<content id>/ (an immutable VALUE; a cross-world create journaled in the target's journal; the same content is the same id, so a re-release is empty), `switch` moves CURRENT (COMPENSABLE: its recorded inverse switches back, CART-1186; gated by the `approve-deploy` DECISION), then the `deploy-health` PREMISE (automated review). Gates: `target-write` + `approve-deploy` (approve=yes, or a remembered decision). rollback=1: a failed health check compensates the switch and undoes the release — the target byte-for-byte as it was. Compensation in general: a compensable verb's `compensate(args, entry)` returns the inverse INVOCATION; rollback runs it through the same step executor. CART-0154 / CART-1186 |\n| Compose write verbs toward a goal and stop ONLY on a genuine decision (a tactic: then / first / try / repeat / each) | `local tactic = require 'cartograph.tactic'; local T = tactic.T` → `tactic.run(store, T.seq(T.step('moveset', {seed_refs, dest}, {'surface'}), T.step('replace', {ref, text}, {'supplied-text'})), { apply = true, oracle = fn })` → `status` done / previewed / stopped (a decision, with `options` + `fixes`) / failed (class, where); `residue`, `work_orders` (every unbuilt stop), `rolled_back`. A DRY run (`apply = false`, the default) CHAINS OVERLAY WORLDS: each journaled step's staged texts become a virtual graph (`world.edit`) the next step plans in, so the whole term previews — `preview` = { [rel] = final text }, `worlds` = how many were stacked, the caller's graph comes back afterwards; a dry `repeat` converges on its own effect; a failed dry alternative drops its world; after a non-journaled step the rest is `underivable` (CART-1160 step 3). FORWARD RECOVERY: a run that stops KEEPS its completed steps (`completed`, each with its `effect`) and resuming is RE-RUNNING the same term with the decision answered in the step's `accept` list — every verb is goal-checked, so a completed step is `empty` the second time (`resumable`); `on_stop = 'rollback'` undoes a stopped run only over journaled writes. Verbs declare `effect` (journaled / compensable / irreversible; undeclared = irreversible, never inside first/try/repeat) and `rerun = 'empty'`. Verbs: `compose.VERBS` (moveset, replace, annotate, clonemerge), addressed by durable ref. One step alone: `tactic.step(store, {verb, args, accept}, {apply})` (compose's recipes run on it). CART-1152 |\n| Did you mean? — correct a refused invocation's argument (a slipped name, a wrong file, a symbol that MOVED or was RENAMED) | in a tactic: a plan-phase `ill-posed`/`stale` refusal asks `require('cartograph.correct').suggest(store, spec, args)` (the adapter declares `correct = { ref = 'ref' }` / `{ seed_refs = 'refs' }`) and keeps the candidates the VERB accepts (a dry step, no failing guard). ★ AUTOMATIC ONLY ON PROVENANCE: a stale ref to a symbol THIS run's own step moved (the adapter's `provides`; also on a resume, where the move is empty) is corrected, and listed in `result.corrections`. Everything INFERRED (edit distance, the witness — a SHAPE hash, CART-1154 —, the same name elsewhere, a same-shaped rename) is a DECISION whose options carry the corrected args (`source` moved|near|renamed|elsewhere, `CONTRADICTS` when the ref's witness disagrees). A witnessed ref whose symbol is GONE