ack=1: a failed health check compensates the switch and undoes the release — the target byte-for-byte as it was. Compensation in general: a compensable verb's `compensate(args, entry)` returns the inverse INVOCATION; rollback runs it through the same step executor. CART-0154 / CART-1186 |\n| Compose write verbs toward a goal and stop ONLY on a genuine decision (a tactic: then / first / try / repeat / each) | `local tactic = require 'cartograph.tactic'; local T = tactic.T` → `tactic.run(store, T.seq(T.step('moveset', {seed_refs, dest}, {'surface'}), T.step('replace', {ref, text}, {'supplied-text'})), { apply = true, oracle = fn })` → `status` done / previewed / stopped (a decision, with `options` + `fixes`) / failed (class, where); `residue`, `work_orders` (every unbuilt stop), `rolled_back`. A DRY run (`apply = false`, the default) CHAINS OVERLAY WORLDS: each journaled step's staged texts become a virtual graph (`world.edit`) the next step plans in, so the whole term previews — `preview` = { [rel] = final text }, `worlds` = how many were stacked, the caller's graph comes back afterwards; a dry `repeat` converges on its own effect; a failed dry alternative drops its world; after a non-journaled step the rest is `underivable` (CART-1160 step 3). FORWARD RECOVERY: a run that stops KEEPS its completed steps (`completed`, each with its `effect`) and resuming is RE-RUNNING the same term with the decision answered in the step's `accept` list — every verb is goal-checked, so a completed step is `empty` the second time (`resumable`); `on_stop = 'rollback'` undoes a stopped run only over journaled writes. Verbs declare `effect` (journaled / compensable / irreversible; undeclared = irreversible, never inside first/try/repeat) and `rerun = 'empty'`. Verbs: `compose.VERBS` (moveset, replace, annotate, clonemerge), addressed by durable ref. One step alone: `tactic.step(store, {verb, args, accept}, {apply})` (compose's recipes run on it). CART-1152 |\n| Did you mean? — correct a refused invocation's argument (a slipped name, a wrong file, a symbol that MOVED or was RENAMED) | in a tactic: a plan-phase `ill-posed`/`stale` refusal asks `require('cartograph.correct').suggest(store, spec, args)` (the adapter declares `correct = { ref = 'ref' }` / `{ seed_refs = 'refs' }`) and keeps the candidates the VERB accepts (a dry step, no failing guard). ★ AUTOMATIC ONLY ON PROVENANCE: a stale ref to a symbol THIS run's own step moved (the adapter's `provides`; also on a resume, where the move is empty) is corrected, and listed in `result.corrections`. Everything INFERRED (edit distance, the witness — a SHAPE hash, CART-1154 —, the same name elsewhere, a same-shaped rename) is a DECISION whose options carry the corrected args (`source` moved|near|renamed|elsewhere, `CONTRADICTS` when the ref's witness disagrees). A witnessed ref whose symbol is GONE fails `stale` and lists near names for information. `opts.correct = 'ask' | 'off'`. Edit distance: `require('cartograph.near').within(key, set)` (all candidates, ties kept) |\n| Why did a write verb STOP, and what should a tactic do next? (the stop CLASS: decision / unbuilt / frontier / ill-posed / stale / empty / informational / environment) | a refusal's third return (`local plan, why, class = verb.plan(…)`; before the write, `txn.stage(store, plan)` — the ONE staging preview and apply share — answers `nil, why, class`; optapply-family CODES map via `require('cartograph.hazard').CODE_CLASS`); a hazard row's `.class`; on the wire `refusal.class` and the hazards note's `evidence.hazards[i].class` (`hazard.plain(list)` is the JSON-safe form — a raw row encodes as `[]`). Vocabulary: `hazard.CLASSES`; fenced by `tests/stopclass_spec.lua` (CART-1152) |\n| Read a metaprogram's sites: what a site of a declared shape GENERATES, with the site on every fact | `require('cartograph.generators').read(gen, troot, src, file)` → facts, refusals (shape / hole / context), selected; declarations: `spec.<lang>.generators`, `pack